{
  "case_id": "2006-05-983",
  "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. ANDRE: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: This case asks the Court to decide to what extent non-lawyer parents of a child with a disability may litigate an IDEA case pro se in Federal court. Under two distinct theories, the answer to that question should be without limitation. But I would like to focus today on petitioner's primary and first theory, which is that parents are real parties in interest in IDEA suits regardless of the claims being asserted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: They are an aggrieved party for purposes of the administrative process. The question is whether that -- when that is done, whether they also constitute an aggrieved party. And one of the -- one of the points made by the other side is that there is an express provision for proceeding without counsel at the administrative level, and there's no provision for proceeding without counsel in court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0000-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: Was their an argument at any point in this case that the claim was frivolous?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Salmons",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The definition says that the term free appropriate public education means special education services provided, quote, without charge and at no cost to parents."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'm not following you. Where is this provision? 1401 what?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The common law rule banning parental pro se representation is as longstanding as it is pervasive."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Your Honor, I would classify that as not a right, it's a remedy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you classify right to reimbursement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Bergeron",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Our position is it would be paid to the child. The child would be the party that could bring that claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Oh, well -- right. I'm sorry. Then you go ahead. I thought I heard you say that the problem is that the parent didn't have a right taken away by the hearing officer, and that's why the parent can't go to court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: We don't have any First Circuit numbers --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Are you claiming that hiring an attorney would be a cost, if the phrase \"at no cost to the parent,\" if they have to hire an attorney, that the cost --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "could be, could be reached based on looking at the addition of attorney's fees provision and the timing of the Maroni decision in the First Circuit."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "05d47561fd0f2c28d42338d0046f44931a8b4870c47235a8defce500d886a8ab",
      "evidence_id": "ev-05d47561fd0f-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that this Court's spending clause jurisprudence is concerned with providing clear notice to states with respect to liability and certain fiscal obligations."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2006-05-983",
      "confidence": 0.0,
